==English==
{{wikipedia|dab=Epistolary}}

===Etymology===
1650s, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|épistolaire|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|epistolaris|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|epistola||lang=la|letter}} (English {{term|epistle|lang=en}}),<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref> from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|ἐπιστολή|lang=grc}} from {{term|ἐπιστέλλω||I send a message|lang=grc}} from {{term|ἐπί||upon|lang=grc}} + {{term|στέλλω||I prepare, send|lang=grc}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|e|pis|to|la|ry|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# a Christian liturgical book containing set readings for church services from the [[New Testament]] [[Epistles]].

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# of or relating to [[letter]]s, or the [[writing]] of letters
# carried on by [[written]] [[correspondence]]
# in the manner of written correspondence
#: '''''epistolary''' style''
#: ''an '''epistolary''' novel''

